Sample Project Explanation (DevOps/Kubernetes)
I worked on a production-grade microservices platform deployed on Kubernetes (AKS).
We had around 18 microservices. CI/CD was done using Azure DevOps, deployments with Helm, monitoring via Prometheus + Grafana, and logging via Loki.
My responsibilities were CI/CD automation, Kubernetes deployments, scaling (HPA), secret management (Key Vault + External Secrets), and production troubleshooting.
A major challenge was handling load spikes — we tuned resource requests and enabled autoscaling which improved performance and reduced cost.
Outcome: Faster releases, fewer manual tasks, and better reliability in production.

